.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_VBOXVFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_vboxvfs
.Nd mount a VirtualBox shared folder
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl r | Fl w
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar share
.Ar node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility attaches the VirtualBox shared folder named
.Ar share
to the directory
.Ar node ,
using the
.Nm vboxvfs
file system.
A shared folder is a directory on the host that the VirtualBox hypervisor
exports to a guest; it has to be defined in the settings of the virtual
machine first, for example with
.Bd -literal -offset indent
VBoxManage sharedfolder add <vm> --name <share> --hostpath <directory>
.Ed
on the host.
The guest additions kernel module
.Nm vboxguest
must be loaded; the
.Nm vboxvfs
module is loaded automatically.
.Pp
Files and directories on a shared folder belong to the host user that runs
the virtual machine, and the host performs every operation with that user's
permissions.
The host does not report user or group identifiers, so inside the guest all
files appear to be owned by the user and group given with the
.Cm uid
and
.Cm gid
options.
By default the permission bits shown are the ones the host reports for each
file; they can be overridden for the whole mount with
.Cm file_mode
and
.Cm dir_mode .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d
Print the options that would be passed to
.Xr nmount 2
and exit without mounting anything.
This is a debugging aid.
.It Fl r
Mount the file system read-only, the same as
.Fl o Cm ro .
.It Fl w
Mount the file system read-write
.Pq the default ,
the same as
.Fl o Cm rw .
.It Fl o Ar options
Options are specified with a
.Fl o
flag followed by a comma separated string of options.
See the
.Xr mount 8
man page for the generic options such as
.Cm ro ,
.Cm noatime ,
.Cm noexec ,
.Cm nosuid
and
.Cm sync ,
which are passed through to the kernel.
.Pp
Data written in the guest is written behind, the way the NFS client does
it: a complete 64 KiB block is sent to the host at once, a partial one stays
in the buffer cache until a later write completes it,
.Xr close 2 ,
.Xr fsync 2
or
.Xr msync 2 ,
or until the syncer flushes it, which it is asked to do within
.Va vfs.vboxvfs.writedelay
seconds
.Pq default 1 .
With the
.Cm sync
option every
.Xr write 2
reaches the host before it returns.
.Pp
The following options are specific to
.Nm vboxvfs :
.Bl -tag -width "file_mode=mode"
.It Cm uid Ns = Ns Ar user
The owner of all files and directories on the file system, as a user name
or a numeric user ID.
The default is 0
.Pq root .
.It Cm gid Ns = Ns Ar group
The group of all files and directories on the file system, as a group name
or a numeric group ID.
The default is 0
.Pq wheel .
.It Cm file_mode Ns = Ns Ar mode
Show every regular file and symbolic link with the given octal permission
bits instead of the mode reported by the host.
The default of 0 means to use the host's mode.
.It Cm dir_mode Ns = Ns Ar mode
Show every directory with the given octal permission bits instead of the
mode reported by the host.
The default of 0 means to use the host's mode.
.It Cm fmask Ns = Ns Ar mode
Clear the given octal permission bits from the mode of every regular file
and symbolic link.
The default is 0.
.It Cm dmask Ns = Ns Ar mode
Clear the given octal permission bits from the mode of every directory.
The default is 0.
.It Cm ttl Ns = Ns Ar milliseconds
How long cached file attributes stay valid before they are fetched from the
host again.
Changes made on the host become visible in the guest within this time.
The default is 200; a value of 0 disables the cache.
.El
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mount the shared folder
.Dq share
on
.Pa /mnt/share ,
with all files owned by the user and group
.Dq alice :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mount_vboxvfs -o uid=alice,gid=alice share /mnt/share
.Ed
.Pp
The same through
.Xr mount 8 ,
read-only, with directories shown as mode 0755 and files as 0644:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mount -t vboxvfs -o ro,dir_mode=0755,file_mode=0644 share /mnt/share
.Ed
.Pp
An
.Xr fstab 5
entry that mounts the folder at boot.
The
.Cm late
option defers the mount until after the guest additions have been started:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
share	/mnt/share	vboxvfs	rw,uid=1001,gid=1001,late	0	0
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nmount 2 ,
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr umount 8
.Pp
.Lk https://www.virtualbox.org/manual/ "VirtualBox User Manual"
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility first appeared in the
.Fx
Ports Collection in 2017 as part of the VirtualBox guest additions.
This version is a rewrite from 2026.
.Sh CAVEATS
File locks taken with
.Xr flock 2
or
.Xr fcntl 2
are local to the guest; they do not lock the file on the host or in other
guests.
.Pp
The shared folder protocol has no notion of hard links, device nodes,
FIFOs, sockets, file flags, access control lists or extended attributes;
operations that need them fail.
The host clears the set-user-ID, set-group-ID and sticky bits and always
keeps read permission for the owner.
.Pp
Creating symbolic links on a shared folder fails unless the host allows it
for that folder:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
VBoxManage setextradata <vm> \\
    VBoxInternal2/SharedFoldersEnableSymlinksCreate/<share> 1
.Ed
.Pp
Changes made on the host side are only noticed when the cached attributes
expire
.Pq see the Cm ttl No option ;
data written by the guest reaches the host within about a second, or at
.Xr close 2 ,
whichever comes first, unless the file system is mounted with
.Cm sync .
A guest that panics or is powered off loses what was not yet flushed, as
with any write-behind cache.
.Pp
On a Windows host, a file that is open in the guest cannot be removed or
renamed, and file names are not case sensitive.
